GPL-2.0-or-later, a test-only change to QEMU; not part of AfriSovera
TEST EQUIPMENT ONLY (13 Nov 2026, CDC-NCM plan B, architect's N2): a CDC-NCM mode for QEMU's usb-net,
applied to QEMU's own source when the CI builds QEMU (ci.yml), never part of AfriSovera. GitHub's runner
kernel (7.0.0-azure) has no dummy_hcd, so plan A (the runner's Linux NCM gadget) could not run; this is the
weaker kind of evidence, because the same engineer wrote both ends; pc-usbncm grades it together with the
block parser's selftest built from the NCM 1.0 spec. usb-net without ncm=on is unchanged.

